{
  "description": "issue #748: de-duplicating the addressed set is observable in a command's ARGUMENT side effects, not only in its move events. The per-turtle loop evaluates the argument once per addressed turtle, so with `tell [ :a :a ]` — one member, because a turtle command \"applies once for each addressed turtle\" over an \"addressed set\" (spec/turtles-and-sprites.md:113, :44) — the `new_turtle` in argument position spawns exactly ONE turtle (id 2, its own authoritative `turtle_id`) and `:a` moves once, where the pre-#748 direct path evaluated the whole argument twice and spawned two. Every change of the addressed set — here from `tell` — also emits the addressing `primitive` event carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }`, so a consumer can identify the addressed turtle set (issue #766, spec/rendering.md:193); `ask`/`each` emit one again when the previous set is restored, on every exit path.",
